<title>USA: U.S. Q4 current account gap narrowed to $41.38 bln.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q4 current account gap narrowed to $41.38 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. current account, seasonally adjusted, as reported by the Commerce Department.</p>
<p>In Billions of Dlrs/Credits:</p>
<p>    -		   Q4 1996    Q3'96--Rev from	1996</p>
<p> Current Account     -41.38   -47.85   -47.96    -165.10</p>
<p> Goods Balance	 -45.31   -51.87   -51.59    -187.67</p>
<p> Services Balance     18.96    17.59    17.76	73.47</p>
<p> Invest.Income Bal.   -2.41    -4.10    -4.71	-8.42</p>
<p> Total Exports	 268.38   254.41   253.84   1,032.48</p>
<p> Goods Exports	 158.37   150.14   149.94     611.67</p>
<p> Services Exports     57.41    55.57    55.60     223.91</p>
<p>In Billions of Dlrs/Credits:</p>
<p>    -		   Q4 1996    Q3'96--Rev from     1996</p>
<p> Total Imports	-297.14  -292.78  -292.38  -1,155.10</p>
<p> Goods Imports	-203.68  -202.01  -201.53    -799.34</p>
<p> Services Imports    -38.45   -37.98   -37.84    -150.44</p>
<p> Govt. Transfers     -12.62    -9.48    -9.42     -42.47</p>
<p> U.S.Assets Abroad  -114.10   -73.31   -54.68    -306.83</p>
<p> Foreign-HeldAssets  182.05   142.97   124.00     525.05</p>
<p>Net data--Govt. transfers, U.S. assets abroad and foreign-held assets.  </p>
<p>The department said the 1996 current account deficit of $165.1 billion was the largest since a $167.4 billion deficit in 1987.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast a $38.8 billion deficit for the fourth quarter.</p>
</text>
